Usage:
  concord --help
  concord --version
  concord host-lease < JSON stdin      # record this host session's release lease (adapter-invoked)
  concord host-leases                  # print live release leases; prunes stale ones
  concord upgrade < JSON stdin      # apply pending migrations; {"plan":true} reports readiness

Required-field refusals exit 64 before dispatch.
Commands read one strict JSON object from stdin:
  concord invoke < JSON stdin
    required: call_envelope{schema_version, request_id, client_ref, principal_ref, session_ref, agent_ref, directory, worktree, ambient_project_id, scope_version, manifest_digest}, tool, operation, input
    optional: call_envelope.selected_product_id, call_envelope.host_assertion_digest; pre-dispatch decode refusals exit 64; exact fields and exclusions follow the generated agent contracts
    accepted values: tool.operation: concord_product_view.resolve | concord_product_view.snapshot | concord_work_browse.list | concord_work_browse.blocked | concord_work_browse.ready | concord_work_browse.scope | concord_work_browse.messages | concord_work_trace.history | concord_work_trace.observations | concord_work_trace.external_observations | concord_work_trace.relations | concord_work_trace.continuity | concord_work_trace.mutation_result | concord_work_trace.research | concord_work_trace.project_retirement | concord_knowledge.search | concord_knowledge.resolve_note | concord_knowledge.observe_publication | concord_work_define.capture | concord_work_define.revise_intent | concord_work_define.research_pack_create | concord_work_define.research_revision_append | concord_work_define.research_finding_record | concord_work_define.research_source_record | concord_work_define.research_freshness_set | concord_work_define.research_retire | concord_work_define.observation_record | concord_work_define.issue_link_record | concord_work_transition.lifecycle | concord_work_transition.remove | concord_work_transition.workflow_action | concord_work_transition.project_handoff_record | concord_work_transition.project_handoff_consume | concord_work_relate.set_memberships | concord_work_relate.resolve_overlap | concord_work_relate.message_send | concord_work_relate.message_withdraw | concord_work_compact.publish | concord_work_compact.reconcile | concord_domain.list | concord_domain.detail | concord_work_transition.correct_delivery | concord_work_transition.outside_repair | concord_work_transition.outside_repair_reconcile
  concord client-register < JSON stdin
  concord client register < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref, key_id, principal_ref, public_key, capabilities, product_scope, project_scope, agent_scope
    accepted values: capabilities: product_read | work_define | work_transition | work_relate | work_compact | cross_scope | research; public_key: base64 Ed25519; agent_scope: the agent references this client may present
  concord client-policy-update < JSON stdin
  concord client policy-update < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref, principal_ref, capabilities, product_scope, project_scope, agent_scope
    accepted values: capabilities: product_read | work_define | work_transition | work_relate | work_compact | cross_scope | research; agent_scope: the agent references this client may present
  concord client-policy-expand < JSON stdin
  concord client policy-expand < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref
    optional: capabilities, product_scope, project_scope, agent_scope — additive union; every existing grant and the stored principal are preserved (TS5)
    accepted values: capabilities: product_read | work_define | work_transition | work_relate | work_compact | cross_scope | research
  concord client-key-rotate < JSON stdin
  concord client key-rotate < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref, key_id, public_key
    accepted values: public_key: base64 Ed25519
  concord client-revoke < JSON stdin
  concord client revoke < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref
  concord client-show < JSON stdin
  concord client show < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref
    accepted values: read-only; returns registered policy, not session authorization; no key material
  concord product-create < JSON stdin
  concord product create < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, display_name, stage_maturity, stage_audience_commitment, project_id, project_display_name, role
    optional: reason
    accepted values: stage_maturity: prototype | alpha | beta | production | deprecated; stage_audience_commitment: operator_only | limited | public; role: primary | secondary
  concord project-create < JSON stdin
  concord project create < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, display_name, product_id, role, expected_product_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: role: primary | secondary
  concord product-project-add < JSON stdin
  concord product project-add < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, role, expected_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: role: primary | secondary
  concord product-stage-update < JSON stdin
  concord product stage-update < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, stage_maturity, stage_audience_commitment, expected_version
    optional: reason (cite the CD-0091 rung evidence when raising maturity)
    accepted values: stage_maturity: prototype | alpha | beta | production | deprecated; stage_audience_commitment: operator_only | limited | public
  concord product-knowledge-home-designate < JSON stdin
  concord product knowledge-home-designate < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, locator_id, expected_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: locator_id: a canonical_path locator of the member Project
  concord product-knowledge-home-clear < JSON stdin
  concord product knowledge-home-clear < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, expected_version
    optional: reason
  concord project-locator-add < JSON stdin
  concord project locator-add < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, locator_id, kind, value, expected_version
    accepted values: kind: canonical_path | git_remote
  concord project-locator-update < JSON stdin
  concord project locator-update < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, locator_id, kind, value, expected_version
    accepted values: kind: canonical_path | git_remote
  concord project-locator-remove < JSON stdin
  concord project locator-remove < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, locator_id, expected_version
  concord cd-reservations < JSON stdin
  concord cd reservations < JSON stdin
    required: directory
    accepted values: prints the law-addition reservations (law_id, owner_work_id) of the Product that owns the calling checkout; read-only
  concord backup < JSON stdin
    required: destination
    accepted values: destination: absolute clean path that does not yet exist; a manifest is written beside it
  concord receipt < JSON stdin
    required: work_id
    accepted values: prints the product-owned closure receipt markdown (CD-0169) for a completed work item; empty output when the item is not completed
  concord work-shelve < JSON stdin
    required: operation_id, idempotency_key, work_id, expected_version, handoff
    optional: product_id, linear, actor, execution_relinquished, writes_reconciled, effects_reconciled, dependencies_resolved, artifacts_verified
    accepted values: reason is fixed to shelved; no sixth lifecycle state
  concord work-cancel < JSON stdin
    required: operation_id, idempotency_key, work_id, expected_version, handoff
    optional: product_id, linear, actor, execution_relinquished, writes_reconciled, effects_reconciled, dependencies_resolved, artifacts_verified
    accepted values: reason is fixed to cancelled; removal is not archival
  concord session-prepare < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, work_id, agent
    optional: task (max 8192 bytes; none on resume); agent is the active agent; handler refusals exit 2; required-field refusals exit 64
  concord project-resolve < JSON stdin
  concord project resolve < JSON stdin
    required: directory
    optional: worktree (defaults to directory)
  concord restore < JSON stdin
    required: source, destination
    accepted values: source: existing verified backup snapshot path; destination: absolute clean path that does not yet exist and is not the live database
  concord host-lease < JSON stdin
    required: pid
    optional: directory, worktree: session location, named by a breaking-migration refusal; advisory, never interpreted
    accepted values: pid: the host process that holds this release; the core writes the lease under the data root
  concord host-leases < JSON stdin
    required: 
    accepted values: prints the live host leases and prunes stale ones (CD-0111 D2)
  concord upgrade < JSON stdin
    required: 
    optional: plan: read-only readiness report; confirm_sessions_stopped: no session runs on an unfenceable release tree; cancel_cutover_pinned_work: cancel every nonterminal work item selected by the authoring-cutover gate after a verified snapshot inside the maintenance boundary (CD-0218 D5)
    accepted values: applies pending migrations; a breaking step runs only inside the maintenance boundary, which excludes session admission until activation and refuses under a live older session (CD-0111 D3)
